  "remaining": "Shared defined/indirect call and fetch/run orchestration is integrated with scoped host acceptance. Complete initializer/Ready/private fixed-target lifecycle, then separately reviewed public invocation. Preserve accepted private numeric/value/frame/control/memory/bulk/growth/imported-host mechanics and fail-closed bounds. Complete supported-profile conformance/differential/fuzz/resource-limit qualification, source diagnostics, performance/memory/size, native joins, immutable published FieldLog consumption and D3/GA acceptance.",
  "currentCheckpoint": "Underlying fixture-only envelope source and bounded accounting have scoped independent host acceptance: 78 producer methods, 14 exact-source independent methods plus 2 separate test-overlay methods, API1+8, 21,714 fresh candidate comparisons and 32 layouts; root verified 407 source/accounting/review members. No semantic replay, live VM/CLI/target or GA acceptance. Portable CI runner round1 was rejected for ambiguous compiler identity and unrelated diagnostic spans. Corrected runner passes 32 normal/optimized controls and one fresh full Rust1.99 host closure; independent correction review now passes and root accepts the scoped runner. Exact CI wiring is applied; delivery and actual Rust1.98.1 CI remain pending. The earlier complete target still fails Corpus1 CacheWork; no optimization has been accepted from this fixture work.",
  "nextImplementation": "Implement the selected standalone fixture cache-state Rust closure within unchanged source/work/move/caller/lifetime/cleanup bounds, then freeze source and proofs for independent actual-File review. Existing APIs/ABI/report and the immutable envelope pack remain fixed; live VM/target/native work remains unselected.",
  "lifecycleCheckpoint": "The private Swift lifecycle V3 candidate now has root acceptance for its selected host matrix: all 30 rows pass, comprising 1,602 test executions and four compile checks. The four focused contexts pass 23 lifecycle tests each; Swift and all-feature libraries, Frozen regressions and both qualified Node oracle runs also pass. Root verifies all 978 sealed files and all 30 target cleanups. V2\u2019s failed ticket assertion remains preserved; V3 changes its expectation to match retained decoded-cache ownership without changing engine limits. The exact three-file private implementation is now integrated: the full 132-file VM source closure matches the tested candidate, and 23 focused live tests plus Swift-only Clippy pass. Its fresh target is removed. The complete SL matrix, guest table mutation, real full reactor, native execution, FieldLog and GA remain pending.",
  "latestCI": "Host Engine CI 40176959303 for pushed 6b8aba350224ed19f678669bdbea6b359d8de68b passes all three jobs and all 38 steps with zero skips. See verification/github-ci-6b8aba35-engine/terminal-receipt.json. This does not pass native, provider or GA gates.",
  "linuxFixtureRepairCheckpoint": "Exact two-file test-only repair accepted at132-file closure6d4b1deed091d6c0f0a2ae0c101c98afbd0e27fdc3c2b2992a999e08565a3fe8. Production code/limits unchanged.196localpasses and independent3plusnegativecontrols; Linux VM CI nowpasses all12steps including391allfeature/361Swift-only tests inDebugandRelease. No native/fullreactor/GA qualification.",
  "exactReactorDiagnosticCheckpoint": "The exact 53,777,114-byte full Swift FieldLog reactor passes owned validation of 79,832 bodies and 6,505,659 instructions, adoption and runtime construction. Initialization stops at a test-only 64-entry release observer assertion; neither corpus call runs. Root verifies 246 sealed files plus three external bindings. The original failure is preserved, the process group is empty and owned scratch is removed. A narrow test-only observer repair is underway; full-reactor execution, native/public/signed use and GA remain pending. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-diagnostic.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
  "releaseObserverRepairCheckpoint": "The test-only Swift release observer repair is integrated. Root verifies the complete 132-file source closure, a single test-file change and three freshly compiled actual-owner regressions; the isolated four-context suite passes 1,516 executions plus four production checks and four expected cfg-negative checks. The original full-reactor failure remains preserved. A separate exact reactor run is being prepared without changing production bytes or budgets. See docs/swift-release-observer-integration.md.",
  "exactReactorAfterObserverCheckpoint": "The full Swift FieldLog reactor now passes complete owned validation and real initialization. Its first corpus stops at the unchanged CacheWork limit: attempted 64,000,001 of 64,000,000, after 24,054 decodes and 23,990 evictions; the second corpus is unrun. Original consuming cleanup returns primary reservations, tickets and live counters to zero while retaining the failure. Root verifies 214 sealed members and four external bindings; owned scratch is removed. Cache-work optimization analysis is underway without widening bounds. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-after-observer-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
  "cacheResetElisionSelection": "Root selects a narrow private Swift cache candidate after source-bound diagnosis: two redundant 512-slot clearing loops account for at least 24,631,296 credits in the failed target run. A finite actual-cache fixture confirms the cost; this is not measured target CPU attribution or a completion prediction. The additive contract removes only those operations, retaining initialized scratch, explicit pass-boundary checks and all original limits. Implementation and acceptance are pending; no new full-reactor attempt is selected. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-contract.md and verification/swift-cache-reset-elision-root-selection/selection.json.",
  "cacheResetElisionCheckpoint": "Root accepts and integrates the private Swift cache reset elimination: two redundant 512-slot writes are removed, retaining initialized scratch and pass-boundary checks under unchanged limits. The producer matrix passes default/compatibility/all-feature Debug and Release with existing ignores retained; six fresh root live tests pass at VM closure b28da766c84b6353a4511e2fc3fbcb0d4302d5b8a5a74da1ee3d7fb776ca2c11. Owned build targets are removed. A separate unchanged full-reactor attempt is being prepared; no target, native, signed, published FieldLog or GA pass is claimed. See docs/swift-cache-reset-elision-checkpoint.md.",
  "cacheElisionFullTargetCheckpoint": "The separate full Swift reactor attempt after cache reset elimination still reaches CacheWork exhaustion at the unchanged 64,000,000-credit limit, now after 12,971,689 guest instructions. Validation, adoption, construction and Initialize pass; Corpus 2 is skipped and guest/native stdout parity remains unverified. Root verifies 221 final members, 198 preparation inputs and unchanged VM closure; the single attempt exits 101 without timeout/signals, consuming cleanup ends at zero and owned scratch is removed. Bounded remaining-work diagnosis is underway; no retry or limit change is selected. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-after-cache-result.md and verification/swift-exact-reactor-after-cache-root-selection/result-binding.json.",
  "cacheWorkAttributionPreparation": "Remaining Swift cache-work diagnosis verifies the unchanged 132-file closure and 20 packet members. Finite cache controls pass, but existing target counters cannot establish repeated decoding or rank dominant credit costs. Root selects a copied fixed-size test-only credit/decode observer; no algorithm, limit or live source change and no new full-target run is selected. See docs/swift-cache-remaining-work-diagnosis.md and verification/swift-cache-work-attribution-root-selection/preparation.json.",
  "cacheWorkAttributionResult": "One exact full Swift reactor attribution run preserves the prior CacheWork failure and instruction count. All six observer snapshots reconcile: scan/build consumes 62.90% of 64 million credits; resident lookup 19.29%; planning 11.82%. Of 39,432 completed decodes, 38,947 repeat across 485 distinct functions. Consuming cleanup is zero; original failure/false cleanup_empty retained, owned scratch removed and live source unchanged. Bounded decode-planning/lookup optimization assessment is next; no limit increase or full-runtime pass. See docs/swift-cache-work-attribution-result.md.",
  "residentIndexCandidateCheckpoint": "The isolated private Swift resident index passes 626 all-feature Release tests with nine inherited ignores, 29 cache Debug tests, default/compatibility suites, Clippy and scoped formatting. Root verifies all 570 sealed members and the unchanged live VM closure. The finite 256-hit fixture uses 2,048 versus 8,832 credits; fixed cache accounting increases by 840 bytes and foundation accounting by 384 bytes under unchanged limits. Independent review is underway; no live integration or full-reactor retry is selected. See docs/swift-cache-resident-index.md.",
  "residentIndexIntegrationCheckpoint": "The private Swift resident index is integrated at closure 02fd25a32b05cf8c4b10e0f68df029d8851e14610ccecbec772be09af5073f8d. Root verifies 570 producer and 79 independent-review members and passes 32 fresh live tests; all owned commands and target cleanup complete. Independent review finds no actionable defect across original suites, an 8,192-operation reference model and exhaustive constructor/multiple-eviction boundaries. Resource limits remain unchanged. A fresh unchanged full-reactor diagnostic is being prepared; target execution is not yet selected. See docs/swift-cache-resident-index-integration.md.",
  "residentIndexFullTargetResult": "The one exact Swift reactor attempt after resident-index integration passes validation and Initialize, then fails TicketInventory at 87 attempted reservations against the unchanged limit of 86. Root verifies 235 result and 203 preparation members. Construction and Initialize each retain one additional index-buffer ticket; the actual 87th requester is unobserved. Final consuming cleanup reaches zero, original failure flags remain and owned scratch is removed. A finite storage/ownership correction is being evaluated without increasing limits. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-after-resident-index-result.md.",
  "groupedIndexReservationIntegration": "The private Swift grouped-index reservation is integrated at 132-file closure 3ffa1055e462be74c10ee9830bf891bbd196a896dfc7a66dc6befe2a6d9bb70f. Root verifies 179 candidate and 99 independent-review files and passes 32 fresh live tests. The candidate passes 504 regression executions plus formatting/Clippy; independent review passes 21 focused tests, all 832 shorter work budgets and 851 cancellation checkpoints. The finite actual owner recovers one ticket while preserving the 86-ticket limit; cleanup reaches zero. Fresh unchanged full-reactor preparation is underway, with no target retry selected yet. See docs/swift-resident-index-grouped-reservation-integration.md.",
  "groupedIndexFullTargetResult": "One unchanged full Swift reactor attempt after the grouped-index integration passes validation and Initialize, then fails Corpus 1 at CacheWork 64,000,001/64,000,000. It stays within the 86-ticket ceiling (85 live, 86 peak); Corpus 2 is unrun. Root verifies 261 result and 222 preparation members. Final consuming cleanup is zero, original failure flags remain, and 77,766,655 owned scratch bytes are removed. A finite decode-plan reuse diagnosis is next, with no raised limits or new full-target attempt selected. See verification/swift-exact-reactor-after-grouped-index/result.md.",
  "decodePlanReuseCandidate": "The isolated 512-slot decode-plan reuse prototype passes nine dedicated tests in each Debug/Release mode, twelve inherited tests and three paired Frozen controls. Repeated large-body charged work falls 36.53%, while tiny-body work rises 2.14%; fixed cache reservation grows 29,008 bytes under unchanged limits. Root verifies 704 files and seven external bindings. Independent finite accounting and exact-phase review is underway; full regression, live integration and another full-reactor attempt are not selected. See docs/swift-decode-plan-reuse-diagnosis.md.",
  "decodePlanReuseAccountingReview": "Root accepts the finite decode-plan source/accounting review after verifying 620 sealed files, five external bindings and 4,752 command/source bindings. Thirty-five of 36 named executions pass; the sole original exact-phase fixture failure is preserved and its measured correction passes. No production defect was found; original limits remain unchanged. Isolated full host regressions and measured fixture updates are selected under docs/swift-decode-plan-regression-contract.md. Live integration and another full-reactor attempt remain unselected. See docs/swift-decode-plan-reuse-accounting-review.md and verification/swift-decode-plan-reuse-diagnosis-root-review/accounting-review-acceptance.json.",
  "decodePlanReuseIntegration": "Decode-plan reuse is integrated at 132-file closure 16176e0852fa61cba98acebeb373ee1a6be4c686d0e46ef8bbc144c0527c2cbd. Root verifies 560regression files/five external bindings before mutation, reviews measured three-test-file updates, and passes 340 fresh live private tests with zero ignores. Four complete isolated Debug/Release Swift/full contexts pass 2,314 named executions with nine inherited ignores each. Production cache bytes match independent finite review; all limits unchanged. A small test-only formatting derivative removes all introduced differences; remaining 156 hunks in 17 files match baseline byte-for-byte. Owned scratch removed. Full-reactor preparation is selected, execution pending; prior full failure unchanged. See docs/swift-decode-plan-integration.md and verification/swift-decode-plan-root-integration/acceptance.json.",
  "decodePlanReuseFullTargetObserved": "The single selected full reactor attempt after decode-plan reuse passes validation and Initialize, then fails Corpus 1 at CacheWork 64,000,001 of 64,000,000, function 23610 offset 4154038, after 23,358,291 guest instructions. Corpus 2 unrun. Root verified 311 result members, 242 historical prepared members and 28 pre-cleanup snapshots. Final consuming reservations, live counts and tickets are all zero; no cleanup invariant. Owned scratch removed once, exact compressed executable retained. Raw failure and raw cleanup_empty false are preserved separately. No budget changes or retry. See docs/swift-exact-reactor-after-plan-reuse-result.md; result seal 8f04098c444d63e9d638c32e22297eccdad346222241529ef710c524473e7526.",
  "cacheRemainingWorkDiagnosis": "Root verified 46 sealed diagnosis members, accepted live source unchanged. Exact planning 11,828,480 credits (18.482% of 64M); final failure inside rebuild decoding. Finite actual-cache observer controls pass 164 work prefixes and three cancellations, all owned scratch cleaned. Gross empty-slot/recount opportunity 7,888,384 credits is not net or CPU gain. The separate test-only fixed-memory attribution observer is independently accepted for diagnostic preparation; fresh preparation is underway and no full retry selected. See docs/swift-plan-cache-remaining-work-diagnosis.md.",
  "runtimeDiagnosticsDelivery": "Completed result/diagnosis/native evidence pushed as 6b8aba350224ed19f678669bdbea6b359d8de68b; exact selected 2,927 paths verified and active lanes excluded. Engine CI 40176959303 passes all three jobs and 38 steps with zero skips. Prior 6403eea9 CI passes all three jobs and 38 steps. See verification/github-delivery-runtime-diagnostics/receipt.json.",
